{"seq":1,"direction":"meta","at":"2026-10-21T09:30:28.886Z","frame":{"event":"spawn","pid":59971,"cwd":"/private/tmp/maws-e0a-a2p-nV6nY4/repo-Wn3uGb","bin":"/Users/new/.local/share/claude/versions/2.1.306","args":["-p","--input-format","stream-json","--output-format","stream-json","--verbose","--permission-prompt-tool","stdio","--include-partial-messages","--setting-sources","user,project,local","--permission-mode","default","--forward-subagent-text","--replay-user-messages","--include-hook-events","--session-id","d4709dac-d443-4141-810d-dff9a13e8463","--max-budget-usd","0.01","--append-system-prompt","# Messages to the human (MAWS to-human contract 7)\n\nThe human reads a report, not the transcript: only the messages you send reach them, so everything you want them to read, your answers included, is a message. A message you send before another tool call goes through `mcp__maws__message` (its `text` the message, in Markdown), called in the same response as that tool call: written as text there, it comes back as a paraphrase that never reaches them. Every other message goes inside `<message>…</message>`, one message per span. Where `mcp__maws__message` is missing, a span is the only form.\n\nSend a message when it changes what the human knows or does: the answer to what they asked, a decision or permission only they can give, a blocker or a departure from what they asked, a finding that changes the answer or the plan, and the result when the work ends. A finished step, a passed test, a worker's completion, or what you are about to do next is working record unless one of those applies; what can wait goes into the next message that has to be sent. The request sets the bar: a direct question expects its answer; a long task expects word at those points, and an acknowledgement at the start only if it will run long enough for the human to wonder; anything they did not ask about has to be new to them, consequential, and useful now rather than later. Silence says only that nothing needed sending, so what is unresolved goes in the next message.\n\nAsk for input with `mcp__maws__ask`: `blocking: false` when you can go on working (their answer arrives later as a user message naming the askId), `blocking: true` when your next step needs it. Use the native AskUserQuestion only where `mcp__maws__ask` is missing.\n\nSay what you mean literally, without metaphor. Marks are plain text, never in code.\n\nIn this session `mcp__to-human__message` is the `mcp__maws__message` tool: wherever your instructions name `mcp__to-human__message`, call `mcp__maws__message`, which takes the same input.","--settings","{\"dialogExpiry\":\"never\",\"enabledPlugins\":{\"designer@designer\":false,\"eli5@claude-community\":false},\"outputStyle\":\"default\",\"disableAllHooks\":true,\"env\":{\"MAWS_NATIVE_TO_HUMAN\":\"7\"}}","--debug-file","/private/tmp/maws-e0a-a2p-nV6nY4/debug.log"],"routed":true,"extraEnv":["CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR","ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL","ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN","ENABLE_TOOL_SEARCH","CLAUDE_CODE_FORK_SUBAGENT","CLAUDE_CODE_ENABLE_SDK_FILE_CHECKPOINTING","CLAUDE_CODE_EMIT_SESSION_STATE_EVENTS","TERM","DISABLE_AUTOUPDATER"],"node":"v22.23.2"}}
